#set page(
  paper: "us-letter",
  margin: (
    top: 0.5in,
    bottom: 0.25in,
    right: 0.25in,
    left: 0.25in,
  ),
)

#set table.cell(
  align: horizon,
)

#table(
  columns: (1fr, 1fr, 1fr, 1fr), 
  rows: 2in,
  stroke: 0.5pt,
  inset: 1em,
  // column-gutter: 0pt, 
  // row-gutter: 0pt,
  [Zeus and Poseidon both want the sea-nymph *Thetis*, until a prophecy says her son will be greater than his father. The gods marry her to a mortal, *Peleus*.],
  [At the wedding of *Peleus* and the sea-nymph *Thetis*, *Eris* (Strife), who wasn't invited, throws down a golden apple inscribed "For the fairest."],
  [Hera, Athena, and Aphrodite each claim the apple. *Paris*, a prince of Troy, is made the judge. Aphrodite bribes him with the most beautiful woman in the world.],
  [*Helen*'s many suitors swear the *Oath of Tyndareus*: to defend the marriage of whoever wins her. She marries *Menelaos*, king of Sparta.],
  [Paris comes to Sparta as a *guest* and leaves with Helen and Menelaos's treasure, a crime against _xenia_ (guest-friendship).],
  [Menelaos and his brother *Agamemnon* summon the kings. *Odysseus* feigns madness and *Achilleus* is hidden among girls, but both are found out. About *a thousand ships* gather at *Aulis*.],
  [The winds won't blow. Agamemnon sacrifices his daughter *Iphigeneia* to Artemis, and the fleet sails.],
  [The Greeks land at Troy. For nine years they besiege the city and raid the towns around it. *Chryseis* and *Briseis* are taken as prizes.],
  [*THE ILIAD* begins in the tenth year. Agamemnon must give back Chryseis, so he takes *Briseis* from Achilleus, who withdraws from the fighting in rage.],
  [Achilleus's mother, Thetis, receives a promise from *Zeus* that the Greeks will lose until they honor Achilleus. Zeus helps the Trojans drive back the Greeks in battle.],
  [With the Greeks being driven back to their ships, *Patroklos* goes into battle in Achilleus's armor and is killed by *Hektor*.],
  [Achilleus returns, kills Hektor, and drags his body. *Priam* comes to his tent by night, and Achilleus gives the body back. The _Iliad_ ends with Hektor's funeral.],
  [*Achilleus* is killed by an arrow shot by Paris and guided by Apollo. *Aias* and *Odysseus* compete for his armor. Odysseus wins, and Aias, disgraced, takes his own life.],
  [The Greeks build a *wooden horse* and pretend to sail away. *Sinon* tricks the Trojans into bringing it in. *Laocoön* warns them and is killed by serpents; *Cassandra* is not believed.],
  [Soldiers hidden inside open the gates. *Priam* is killed at an altar, *Astyanax* is thrown from the walls, and *Locrian Aias* drags Cassandra from Athena's temple. *Aeneas* escapes.],
  [The sacrilege of the sack angers the gods. *Athena* sends a storm, and the returning fleet is wrecked and scattered.],
  [*Agamemnon* returns to Mycenae and is murdered by his wife *Klytaimnestra* and her lover *Aigisthos*.],
  [*Odysseus* wanders for *ten years* before reaching home in Ithaka (the _Odyssey_).],)







